# Assets
# docs/assets/ is the media-dir the asset pipeline syncs into, and it is ignored
# whole. The ten files it held were previously un-ignored by name so the README
# could reference them — but the README now serves the hero and icon from docs/
# itself, so nothing in the repo referenced docs/assets/ at all: 6.7 MB of
# duplicates of docs/ and site/src/, plus submission-platform art (Devpost,
# YouTube) whose masters live in the project's own assets/ directory. Ignoring
# the directory whole keeps the sync target working without committing its output.
docs/assets/
build/

# MCPB bundle build output (artefact; manifest.json is the source)
dist-mcpb/
.mcpb-stage/
*.mcpb
